VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- BFD cannot be brought up across this pair.
===========================================================================
DUT side:  `neighbor 2001:db8:10::2 fall-over bfd`  -> **ACCEPTED**
Peer side: `neighbor 2001:db8:10::1 fall-over bfd`  -> % Invalid input
DUT:       `show bfd session`                       -> % Invalid input

So the DUT accepts the BGP-side configuration but exposes no BFD session view,
and the AR4050S will not take the peer half at all. A BFD session needs both
ends; with one end unable to configure it and no way to observe a session on
the other, the case's first assertion ("BFD session should be up and no errors
should be seen") cannot be evaluated.

The AW+ CLI wiki page `neighbor-fall-over-bfd-bgp.md` does not list the IE520
among its platforms. That is consistent with what was measured, but it was
TESTED rather than assumed -- the platform tables are a guide, not a gate
(`ipv6-router-ospf-area.md` also omits the IE520 and that command works).

NOT REACHED: the case's second half (apply an access-list on the peer to kill
the BGP session and confirm BFD detects the failure faster than BGP hold time).
